PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L05U2.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":5,"cefr":"B1a","unit":2,"theme":"Achievements","essential_question":"What does it take to achieve a goal?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1","title":"He Has Trained for Three Years: The Present Perfect with for and since","objectives":["Students will be able to use the present perfect for situations that started in the past and continue now.","Students will be able to choose for (a period) or since (a starting point) and ask How long…?","I can say \"I've lived here since 2020\" and \"He's trained for three years.\"","I can ask \"How long have you known him?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المضارع التام لمواقف بدأت في الماضي وما زالت مستمرة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين for (مدة) وsince (نقطة بداية) والسؤال بـ How long…؟","أستطيع أن أقول I've lived here since 2020 وHe's trained for three years.","أستطيع أن أسأل How long have you known him?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"achieve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈtʃiv/","definition":"to succeed in doing something after trying hard","arabic":"يحقق","example":"She achieved her dream of becoming a pilot.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W01"},{"word":"achievement","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈtʃivmənt/","definition":"something good that you succeed in doing","arabic":"إنجاز","example":"Finishing the marathon was a great achievement.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W02"},{"word":"goal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡoʊl/","definition":"something you want to do in the future","arabic":"هدف","example":"My goal is to read 30 books this year.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W03"},{"word":"effort","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛfɚt/","definition":"hard work you put into doing something","arabic":"جهد","example":"He made a big effort to improve his English.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the present perfect for a situation that started in the past and is still true now: Faisal has been a member since 2023 (and he is still a member).\nUse for + a period of time (for three years, for a long time, for two weeks). Use since + the starting point (since 2023, since Monday, since I was eight).\nAsk How long have/has…? – How long have you known Saad? – I've known him for five years. Don't use the present simple for this meaning: (not: I know him for five years.)\nfor + period: for ten minutes, for a month, for ages\nsince + starting point: since 8 o'clock, since May, since I was a child\nHow long + have/has + subject + past participle?\nNot: I live here since 2020. → I've lived here since 2020.","examples":["My grandparents have lived in Abha since 1980.","I've had this watch for three years.","Lina has been in the chess club since September.","We haven't visited Riyadh for a long time.","How long has your brother worked at the bank?","I've known my best friend since first grade.","The museum has been open for fifty years.","My dad hasn't smoked since 2019 – we're proud of him!"],"common_errors":["✗ I live in Taif since 2015. → ✓ I've lived in Taif since 2015. (Past until now → present perfect.)","✗ I've studied English since three years. → ✓ I've studied English for three years. (A period → for.)","✗ She has been here for Monday. → ✓ She has been here since Monday. (A starting point → since.)","✗ How long do you know him? → ✓ How long have you known him? (How long + present perfect.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم المضارع التام لموقف بدأ في الماضي وما زال مستمرًا: Faisal has been a member since 2023.\nfor + مدة (for three years)، وsince + نقطة البداية (since 2023 / since I was eight).\nلا نقول I live here since 2015، بل I've lived here since 2015.\nالسؤال: How long have you known him? (منذ متى تعرفه؟)"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “He Has Trained for Three Years: The Present Perfect with for and since”. Let’s learn present perfect with for and since; How long…? together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U2-LS1 | He Has Trained for Three Years: The Present Perfect with for and since","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Faisal's Swimming Journey”: Faisal has been a member of the swimming club since 2023. He has trained three times a week for almost three years, and his hard work has paid off. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Faisal has been a member of the swimming club since 2023. He has trained three times a week for almost three years, and his hard work has paid off.","visual":"Image GV-L05-U2-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the present perfect for a situation that started in the past and is still true now: Faisal has been a member since 2023 (and he is still a member). Use for + a period of time (for three years, for a long time, for two weeks). Use since + the starting point (since 2023, since Monday, since I was eight).","on_screen":"for + period: for ten minutes, for a month, for ages • since + starting point: since 8 o'clock, since May, since I was a child • How long + have/has + subject + past participle?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My grandparents have lived in Abha since 1980. I've had this watch for three years. Lina has been in the chess club since September.","on_screen":"My grandparents have lived in Abha since 1980. / I've had this watch for three years. / Lina has been in the chess club since September.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I live in Taif since 2015.” That’s not right. We say: “I've lived in Taif since 2015.” Past until now → present perfect.","on_screen":"✗ I live in Taif since 2015.   ✓ I've lived in Taif since 2015.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I've lived here since 2020.\" Do I live here now? … Think! … Yes. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I've lived here since 2020\" and \"He's trained for three years.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I've lived here since 2020\" and \"He's trained for three years.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present perfect with for and since; How long…?.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم المضارع التام لموقف بدأ في الماضي وما زال مستمرًا: Faisal has been a member since 2023.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I live in Taif since 2015. — الصحيح: I've lived in Taif since 2015.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I've lived here since 2020 وHe's trained for three years."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Faisal's Swimming Journey","body":"Faisal has been a member of the swimming club since 2023. He has trained three times a week for almost three years, and his hard work has paid off.\nLast month, he won a silver medal at the regional championship!\n\"I've wanted to swim in competitions since I was eight,\" he says.\nHis coach, Mr. Hamdan, has known him for a long time. \"Faisal has made great progress,\" the coach explains. \"He hasn't missed a single practice this year.\"\nHis parents have supported him at every competition, and they're very proud of him.\nFaisal has already set a new goal: he wants to join the national team. He hasn't achieved it yet, but he's very ambitious.\n\"I've learned that success needs patience,\" he says with a smile.","word_count":127,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I've known Ziyad ___ six years.","options":["during","for","since","from"],"answer":"for","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."},{"q":"She has worked at the hospital ___ 2018.","options":["for","at","from","since"],"answer":"since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."},{"q":"We ___ in this house since I was born.","options":["have lived","are living","lived","live"],"answer":"have lived","explanation":"Started in the past and continues now → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"من الماضي حتى الآن ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"___ have you had your phone? – For a year.","options":["How often","When","How long","How much"],"answer":"How long","explanation":"How long + have/has + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How long."},{"q":"My uncle hasn't visited us ___ last summer.","options":["from","for","ago","since"],"answer":"since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."},{"q":"They've been married ___ twenty years.","options":["since","for","ago","from"],"answer":"for","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write for or since. Word bank: since, for","items":[{"q":"I've had a cold ______ Sunday.","options":[],"answer":"since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."},{"q":"Majed has played the oud ______ four years.","options":[],"answer":"for","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."},{"q":"We haven't seen a rainbow ______ last winter.","options":[],"answer":"since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write questions with How long…? and answers.","items":[{"q":"you / know your best friend (2019)  (question)","options":[],"answer":"How long have you known your best friend? – Since 2019.","explanation":"How long + have/has + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How long."},{"q":"your dad / work at the airport (ten years)  (question)","options":[],"answer":"How long has your dad worked at the airport? – For ten years.","explanation":"How long + have/has + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How long."},{"q":"Lina / have her cat (last spring)  (question)","options":[],"answer":"How long has Lina had her cat? – Since last spring.","explanation":"How long + have/has + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How long."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about you.","items":[{"q":"I have lived in my house for/since ___.","options":[],"answer":"I have lived in my house since 2017.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I have known my best friend for ___.","options":[],"answer":"I have known my best friend for six years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I have been a student at this school since ___.","options":[],"answer":"I have been a student at this school since Grade 1.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I have had my favorite ___ for ___.","options":[],"answer":"I have had my favorite watch for two years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I haven't eaten ___ for a long time.","options":[],"answer":"I haven't eaten pizza for a long time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Interview for a profile.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 How long…? questions for a classmate.","options":[],"answer":"How long have you lived in Taif? How long have you played football? How long have you known Saad? How long have you had your bike?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write his answers in full sentences.","options":[],"answer":"He has lived in Taif since 2015. He has played football for five years. He has known Saad since Grade 2. He has had his bike for a year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one thing you haven't done for a long time and want to do again.","options":[],"answer":"I haven't visited Al-Ula for three years. I want to go again.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for and since; How long…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"for three years"},{"label":"since 2022"},{"label":"since I was eight"},{"label":"for a long time"},{"label":"just"},{"label":"already"},{"label":"yet"},{"label":"How long…?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My sister has studied English ___ she was five.","options":["from","ago","for","since"],"answer":"since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."},{"q":"I've waited for the bus ___ twenty minutes!","options":["since","for","from","during"],"answer":"for","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."},{"q":"","options":["I've known Lina since kindergarten.","I know Lina since kindergarten.","I knew Lina since kindergarten.","I've known Lina for kindergarten."],"answer":"I've known Lina since kindergarten.","explanation":"Started in the past and continues now → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"من الماضي حتى الآن ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"","options":["How long have you been in this club?","How long you have been in this club?","How long are you in this club?","How long have you be in this club?"],"answer":"How long have you been in this club?","explanation":"How long + have/has + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How long."},{"q":"The shop has been closed ___ Monday.","options":["ago","since","for","from"],"answer":"since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."},{"q":"","options":["My grandpa has the same car for thirty years.","My grandpa had the same car since thirty years.","My grandpa has had the same car for thirty years.","My grandpa has had the same car since thirty years."],"answer":"My grandpa has had the same car for thirty years.","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."},{"q":"We ___ our cousins since Eid.","options":["haven't seen","didn't see","don't see","aren't seeing"],"answer":"haven't seen","explanation":"Started in the past and continues now → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"من الماضي حتى الآن ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"She has been a teacher ___ a long time.","options":["since","ago","for","from"],"answer":"for","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."},{"q":"How long has your brother lived abroad? – ___ 2022.","options":["Ago","Since","For","From"],"answer":"Since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."},{"q":"","options":["They live in Jeddah for ages.","They lived in Jeddah since ages.","They have lived in Jeddah since ages.","They have lived in Jeddah for ages."],"answer":"They have lived in Jeddah for ages.","explanation":"Started in the past and continues now → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"من الماضي حتى الآن ← المضارع التام."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Faisal on a swimming podium holding a silver medal, his coach and proud parents clapping, and a wall calendar showing years of training. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Faisal on a swimming podium holding a silver medal, his coach and proud parents clapping, and a wall calendar showing years of training"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present perfect with for and since; How long…?, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present perfect with for and since"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows achieve (to succeed in doing something after trying hard); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing achieve: to succeed in doing something after trying hard"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows achievement (something good that you succeed in doing); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing achievement: something good that you succeed in doing"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows goal (something you want to do in the future); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing goal: something you want to do in the future"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows effort (hard work you put into doing something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing effort: hard work you put into doing something"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W01","script":"achieve. achieve. She achieved her dream of becoming a pilot.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W02","script":"achievement. achievement. Finishing the marathon was a great achievement.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W03","script":"goal. goal. My goal is to read 30 books this year.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-W04","script":"effort. effort. He made a big effort to improve his English.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-T1","script":"Faisal has been a member of the swimming club since 2023. He has trained three times a week for almost three years, and his hard work has paid off. Last month, he won a silver medal at the regional championship! \"I've wanted to swim in competitions since I was eight,\" he says. His coach, Mr. Hamdan, has known him for a long time. \"Faisal has made great progress,\" the coach explains. \"He hasn't missed a single practice this year.\" His parents have supported him at every competition, and they're very proud of him. Faisal has already set a new goal: he wants to join the national team. He hasn't achieved it yet, but he's very ambitious. \"I've learned that success needs patience,\" he says with a smile.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “He Has Trained for Three Years: The Present Perfect with for and since”. Let’s learn present perfect with for and since; How long…? together. Listen to the start of “Faisal's Swimming Journey”: Faisal has been a member of the swimming club since 2023. He has trained three times a week for almost three years, and his hard work has paid off. Look at the green words. We use the present perfect for a situation that started in the past and is still true now: Faisal has been a member since 2023 (and he is still a member). Use for + a period of time (for three years, for a long time, for two weeks). Use since + the starting point (since 2023, since Monday, since I was eight). Here are some examples. My grandparents have lived in Abha since 1980. I've had this watch for three years. Lina has been in the chess club since September. Be careful! Some learners say: “I live in Taif since 2015.” That’s not right. We say: “I've lived in Taif since 2015.” Past until now → present perfect. Quick check: \"I've lived here since 2020.\" Do I live here now? … Think! … Yes. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I've lived here since 2020\" and \"He's trained for three years.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2","title":"I've Just Won! just, already and yet","objectives":["Students will be able to use just (a short time ago) and already (sooner than expected) in positive sentences.","Students will be able to use yet in negatives and questions and put each word in the right position.","I can say \"I've just finished\" and \"She's already won two medals.\"","I can ask \"Have you finished yet?\" and say \"I haven't decided yet.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام just (منذ قليل) وalready (قبل المتوقع) في الإثبات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام yet في النفي والسؤال ووضع كل كلمة في مكانها الصحيح.","أستطيع أن أقول I've just finished وShe's already won two medals.","أستطيع أن أسأل Have you finished yet? وأقول I haven't decided yet."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"progress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɑˌɡrɛs/","definition":"getting better at something","arabic":"تقدّم","example":"You've made great progress in math.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W01"},{"word":"award","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈwɔrd/","definition":"a prize for doing something well","arabic":"جائزة","example":"Noura won an award for her short story.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W02"},{"word":"medal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛdəl/","definition":"a round piece of metal given as a prize","arabic":"ميدالية","example":"He won a gold medal in swimming.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W03"},{"word":"certificate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɚˈtɪfɪkət/","definition":"an official paper that shows you did something","arabic":"شهادة","example":"Every student received a certificate at the end of the course.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"just = a very short time ago. It goes between have/has and the past participle: I've just finished my project.\nalready = before now, or sooner than expected. It usually goes between have/has and the past participle: She's already won two medals!\nyet = until now (used in negatives and questions). It goes at the end: I haven't decided yet. Have you finished yet?\nhave/has + just + past participle\nhave/has + already + past participle\nhaven't/hasn't + past participle + … + yet\nHave/Has + subject + past participle + … + yet?","examples":["I've just seen the results – I passed!","Noura has already written three chapters of her story.","The bus hasn't arrived yet.","Have you chosen your project yet?","My brother has just passed his driving test.","We've already collected 200 books for the library.","The new mall hasn't opened yet.","Has the match started yet? – Yes, it's just started."],"common_errors":["✗ I have finished yet. → ✓ I've already finished. / I haven't finished yet. (yet is for negatives and questions.)","✗ She has won already the prize. → ✓ She has already won the prize. (already goes before the past participle.)","✗ I've finished just my homework. → ✓ I've just finished my homework. (just goes before the past participle.)","✗ Did you finish yet? → ✓ Have you finished yet? (With yet, use the present perfect.)"],"arabic":"just تعني «للتو» وتأتي بين have/has والتصريف الثالث: I've just finished.\nalready تعني «بالفعل / من قبل» وتأتي في المكان نفسه: She's already won two medals.\nyet تعني «حتى الآن» وتأتي في آخر جملة النفي والسؤال: I haven't decided yet. / Have you finished yet?"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I've Just Won! just, already and yet”. Let’s learn present perfect with just, already and yet together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U2-LS2 | I've Just Won! just, already and yet","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: We've just arrived. • I've already read this book. He hasn't finished yet. Have you packed yet? – Yes, I've already packed. / No, not yet.","on_screen":"We've just arrived. • I've already read this book. | He hasn't finished yet. | Have you packed yet? – Yes, I've already packed. / No, not yet.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"just = a very short time ago. It goes between have/has and the past participle: I've just finished my project. already = before now, or sooner than expected. It usually goes between have/has and the past participle: She's already won two medals!","on_screen":"have/has + just + past participle • have/has + already + past participle • haven't/hasn't + past participle + … + yet","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I've just seen the results – I passed! Noura has already written three chapters of her story. The bus hasn't arrived yet.","on_screen":"I've just seen the results – I passed! / Noura has already written three chapters of her story. / The bus hasn't arrived yet.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I have finished yet.” That’s not right. We say: “I've already finished. / I haven't finished yet.” yet is for negatives and questions.","on_screen":"✗ I have finished yet.   ✓ I've already finished. / I haven't finished yet.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I've just finished.\" When did I finish? … Think! … A very short time ago. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I've just finished\" and \"She's already won two medals.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I've just finished\" and \"She's already won two medals.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present perfect with just, already and yet.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","just تعني «للتو» وتأتي بين have/has والتصريف الثالث: I've just finished.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I have finished yet. — الصحيح: I've already finished. / I haven't finished yet.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I've just finished وShe's already won two medals."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I've ___ finished my homework. Can I go out now?","options":["yet","ever","since","just"],"answer":"just","explanation":"just = a short time ago (have + just + past participle).","explanation_ar":"just للتو."},{"q":"Have you done your project ___?","options":["yet","already","just","still"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"She's ___ read the book, so she doesn't want to see the film.","options":["since","yet","ever","already"],"answer":"already","explanation":"already = sooner than expected (have + already + past participle).","explanation_ar":"already بالفعل."},{"q":"The guests haven't arrived ___.","options":["ever","yet","just","already"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"","options":["We've bought already the tickets.","We've already bought the tickets.","We've bought the tickets already yet.","We already have the tickets bought."],"answer":"We've already bought the tickets.","explanation":"Put just/already before the past participle; yet at the end.","explanation_ar":"مكان الكلمة."},{"q":"","options":["He just has left.","He's left yet.","He's just left.","He's left just."],"answer":"He's just left.","explanation":"Put just/already before the past participle; yet at the end.","explanation_ar":"مكان الكلمة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write just, already or yet. Word bank: just, yet, already","items":[{"q":"Hurry up! The film has ______ started.","options":[],"answer":"already","explanation":"already = sooner than expected (have + already + past participle).","explanation_ar":"already بالفعل."},{"q":"I'm so happy! I've ______ received my certificate.","options":[],"answer":"just","explanation":"just = a short time ago (have + just + past participle).","explanation_ar":"just للتو."},{"q":"Has the teacher marked our tests ______?","options":[],"answer":"yet","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Look at Sara's to-do list. Write sentences.","items":[{"q":"research (✔ – done last week)  (already)","options":[],"answer":"Sara has already done the research.","explanation":"already = sooner than expected (have + already + past participle).","explanation_ar":"already بالفعل."},{"q":"poster (✔ – done 5 minutes ago)  (just)","options":[],"answer":"Sara has just finished the poster.","explanation":"just = a short time ago (have + just + past participle).","explanation_ar":"just للتو."},{"q":"presentation (✘)  (yet)","options":[],"answer":"Sara hasn't practiced the presentation yet.","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about your progress.","items":[{"q":"Have you finished your homework yet?","options":[],"answer":"No, I haven't finished it yet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What have you just done?","options":[],"answer":"I've just answered question 3.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you've already done this week: ___","options":[],"answer":"I've already cleaned my room this week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you haven't done yet this year: ___","options":[],"answer":"I haven't visited the new museum yet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Have you decided your goal for next year yet?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I've already decided: I want to join the debate team.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My goal tracker.","items":[{"q":"Choose a goal. Write 2 things you've already done for it.","options":[],"answer":"Goal: run 5 km. I've already bought running shoes. I've already run 2 km.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 things you haven't done yet.","options":[],"answer":"I haven't run 5 km yet. I haven't joined a running club yet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one piece of news with just.","options":[],"answer":"I've just beaten my best time!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with just, already and yet correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and present perfect with just, already and yet.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"I / know / my best friend / since first grade"},{"cue":"she / play / the piano / for five years"},{"cue":"we / live / here / since 2020"},{"cue":"he / just / finish / his project"},{"cue":"they / already / win / two medals"},{"cue":"you / finish / homework / yet?"},{"cue":"How long / your dad / work / there?"},{"cue":"I / not / decide / yet"},{"cue":"my team / train / for months"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Look! It's ___ stopped raining.","options":["yet","since","ever","just"],"answer":"just","explanation":"just = a short time ago (have + just + past participle).","explanation_ar":"just للتو."},{"q":"Have you met the new teacher ___?","options":["ever since","yet","already","just"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"My brother has ___ eaten all the cookies!","options":["yet","already","since","ever"],"answer":"already","explanation":"already = sooner than expected (have + already + past participle).","explanation_ar":"already بالفعل."},{"q":"","options":["I haven't read the news yet.","I haven't read yet the news.","I have read the news yet.","I didn't read yet the news."],"answer":"I haven't read the news yet.","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"","options":["She's finished her exam yet.","She already has finished her exam.","She's already finished her exam.","She's finished already her exam yet."],"answer":"She's already finished her exam.","explanation":"Put just/already before the past participle; yet at the end.","explanation_ar":"مكان الكلمة."},{"q":"","options":["Has the bus yet arrived?","Did the bus arrive yet?","Has arrived the bus yet?","Has the bus arrived yet?"],"answer":"Has the bus arrived yet?","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"We've ___ moved to a new house. Come and visit!","options":["ever","yet","just","since"],"answer":"just","explanation":"just = a short time ago (have + just + past participle).","explanation_ar":"just للتو."},{"q":"Don't tell me the ending! I haven't finished the book ___.","options":["yet","already","just","ever"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"","options":["I just have spoken to the coach.","I've spoken just to the coach.","I've spoke just to the coach.","I've just spoken to the coach."],"answer":"I've just spoken to the coach.","explanation":"Put just/already before the past participle; yet at the end.","explanation_ar":"مكان الكلمة."},{"q":"Have you packed for the trip yet? – Yes, I've ___ packed.","options":["since","already","ever","yet"],"answer":"already","explanation":"already = sooner than expected (have + already + past participle).","explanation_ar":"already بالفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A school project checklist on a board with ticks and empty boxes: \"research – already done\", \"poster – just finished\", \"presentation – not yet\", while Lina and Sara check it. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school project checklist on a board with ticks and empty boxes: \"research – already done\", \"poster – just finished\", \"presentation – not yet\", while Lina and Sara check it"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present perfect with just, already and yet: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Achievements”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present perfect with just, already and yet: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Achievements”"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows progress (getting better at something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing progress: getting better at something"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows award (a prize for doing something well); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing award: a prize for doing something well"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows medal (a round piece of metal given as a prize); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing medal: a round piece of metal given as a prize"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows certificate (an official paper that shows you did something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing certificate: an official paper that shows you did something"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W01","script":"progress. progress. You've made great progress in math.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W02","script":"award. award. Noura won an award for her short story.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W03","script":"medal. medal. He won a gold medal in swimming.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-W04","script":"certificate. certificate. Every student received a certificate at the end of the course.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I've Just Won! just, already and yet”. Let’s learn present perfect with just, already and yet together. Remember these patterns: We've just arrived. • I've already read this book. He hasn't finished yet. Have you packed yet? – Yes, I've already packed. / No, not yet. just = a very short time ago. It goes between have/has and the past participle: I've just finished my project. already = before now, or sooner than expected. It usually goes between have/has and the past participle: She's already won two medals! Here are some examples. I've just seen the results – I passed! Noura has already written three chapters of her story. The bus hasn't arrived yet. Be careful! Some learners say: “I have finished yet.” That’s not right. We say: “I've already finished. / I haven't finished yet.” yet is for negatives and questions. Quick check: \"I've just finished.\" When did I finish? … Think! … A very short time ago. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I've just finished\" and \"She's already won two medals.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3","title":"Make Progress, Do Your Best: Achievement Collocations","objectives":["Students will be able to use achievement collocations with make, do, win, achieve and set.","Students will be able to use word families such as succeed → success → successful.","I can say \"make progress\", \"do my best\" and \"achieve a goal\".","I can choose between succeed, success and successful."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام متلازمات الإنجاز مع make وdo وwin وachieve وset.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام عائلات الكلمات مثل succeed → success → successful.","أستطيع أن أقول make progress وdo my best وachieve a goal.","أستطيع أن أختار بين succeed وsuccess وsuccessful."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"skill","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skɪl/","definition":"the ability to do something well","arabic":"مهارة","example":"Typing fast is a useful skill.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W01"},{"word":"practice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpræktəs/","definition":"doing something again and again to get better","arabic":"تدريب / ممارسة","example":"Practice makes perfect!","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W02"},{"word":"succeed","pos":"verb","ipa":"/səkˈsid/","definition":"to do what you tried to do","arabic":"ينجح","example":"If you keep trying, you will succeed.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W03"},{"word":"success","pos":"noun","ipa":"/səkˈsɛs/","definition":"achieving what you wanted","arabic":"نجاح","example":"The science fair was a big success.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W04"},{"word":"challenge","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃæləndʒ/","definition":"something difficult that tests your ability","arabic":"تحدٍّ","example":"Climbing the mountain was a real challenge.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W05"},{"word":"proud","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/praʊd/","definition":"feeling happy about something you or someone else did","arabic":"فخور","example":"My parents are proud of my results.","image_id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"make and do are often confused. make goes with: progress, an effort, a mistake, a decision, a plan, a difference. do goes with: your best, well, research, homework, exercise, a project.\nOther achievement partners: set a goal, achieve a goal, reach a goal, win an award / a medal / a prize, earn a certificate, face a challenge, develop a skill.\nWord families help you write correctly: succeed (verb) → success (noun) → successful (adjective) → successfully (adverb).\nWord families: achieve: achievement (n), achievable (adj) | succeed: success (n), successful (adj), successfully (adv) | pride: proud (adj), proudly (adv) | challenge: challenging (adj), challenge (v) | practice: practical (adj), practice (v)\nCollocations/phrases: make progress • make an effort • make a mistake • make a decision • make a difference | do your best • do well • do research • do exercise • do a project | set / achieve / reach a goal • win a medal/award • earn a certificate • face a challenge • develop a skill","examples":["Rakan has made a lot of progress in English.","Just do your best in the exam.","Everyone makes mistakes – that's how we learn.","Lina set a goal to read one book a week.","Our team won an award for the best project.","The course helped me develop new skills.","The event was a big success.","She finished the race successfully."],"common_errors":["✗ I did a mistake. → ✓ I made a mistake. (mistake → make.)","✗ He made his best. → ✓ He did his best. (do your best.)","✗ She is very success. → ✓ She is very successful. (Adjective → successful.)","✗ We gained a medal. → ✓ We won a medal. (win a medal.)"],"arabic":"make مع: progress (تقدم) وan effort (جهد) وa mistake (خطأ) وa decision (قرار).\ndo مع: your best (أفضل ما لديك) وwell وresearch وexercise وhomework.\nset/achieve a goal (يضع/يحقق هدفًا) وwin a medal (يفوز بميدالية).\nsucceed (فعل) ← success (اسم) ← successful (صفة) ← successfully (ظرف)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Make Progress, Do Your Best: Achievement Collocations”. Let’s learn achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U2-LS3 | Make Progress, Do Your Best: Achievement Collocations","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. skill: the ability to do something well. practice: doing something again and again to get better. succeed: to do what you tried to do.","on_screen":"skill | practice | succeed","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"make and do are often confused. make goes with: progress, an effort, a mistake, a decision, a plan, a difference. do goes with: your best, well, research, homework, exercise, a project. Other achievement partners: set a goal, achieve a goal, reach a goal, win an award / a medal / a prize, earn a certificate, face a challenge, develop a skill.","on_screen":"achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Rakan has made a lot of progress in English. Just do your best in the exam. Everyone makes mistakes – that's how we learn.","on_screen":"Rakan has made a lot of progress in English. / Just do your best in the exam. / Everyone makes mistakes – that's how we learn.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I did a mistake.” That’s not right. We say: “I made a mistake.” mistake → make.","on_screen":"✗ I did a mistake.   ✓ I made a mistake.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we \"make\" or \"do\" a mistake? … Think! … *make* a mistake. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"make progress\", \"do my best\" and \"achieve a goal\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"make progress\", \"do my best\" and \"achieve a goal\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","make مع: progress (تقدم) وan effort (جهد) وa mistake (خطأ) وa decision (قرار).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I did a mistake. — الصحيح: I made a mistake.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول make progress وdo my best وachieve a goal."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Don't worry if you ___ a mistake.","options":["make","take","do","have"],"answer":"make","explanation":"make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"Just ___ your best, and you'll be fine.","options":["make","have","do","give"],"answer":"do","explanation":"do + your best / well / research / exercise.","explanation_ar":"do مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"She has ___ a lot of progress this year.","options":["made","done","got","had"],"answer":"made","explanation":"make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"Our class ___ an award for the cleanest classroom.","options":["gained","earned up","took","won"],"answer":"won","explanation":"Use the right achievement partner (set, achieve, win, earn).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The concert was a great ___.","options":["successfully","successful","succeed","success"],"answer":"success","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."},{"q":"He ___ to finish the race in under an hour.","options":["success","succeeded","successful","successfully"],"answer":"succeeded","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to the words.","items":[{"q":"set","options":["a new skill","a gold medal","an important decision","a difficult challenge","research for a project","a goal for the new year"],"answer":"a goal for the new year","explanation":"set → a goal for the new year. make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"make","options":["a new skill","a gold medal","an important decision","a difficult challenge","research for a project","a goal for the new year"],"answer":"an important decision","explanation":"make → an important decision. make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"do","options":["a new skill","a gold medal","an important decision","a difficult challenge","research for a project","a goal for the new year"],"answer":"research for a project","explanation":"do → research for a project. make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"win","options":["a new skill","a gold medal","an important decision","a difficult challenge","research for a project","a goal for the new year"],"answer":"a gold medal","explanation":"win → a gold medal. make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"face","options":["a new skill","a gold medal","an important decision","a difficult challenge","research for a project","a goal for the new year"],"answer":"a difficult challenge","explanation":"face → a difficult challenge. make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"develop","options":["a new skill","a gold medal","an important decision","a difficult challenge","research for a project","a goal for the new year"],"answer":"a new skill","explanation":"develop → a new skill. make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your achievements and goals.","items":[{"q":"A goal I have set for myself: ___","options":[],"answer":"I've set a goal to learn 500 new English words.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A subject where I've made progress: ___","options":[],"answer":"I've made progress in science this term.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A skill I want to develop: ___","options":[],"answer":"I want to develop my public speaking skills.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An achievement I'm proud of: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm proud that I won second prize in the reading contest.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A challenge I've faced: ___","options":[],"answer":"I've faced the challenge of moving to a new school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My achievement poster.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a person you admire using achievement collocations.","options":[],"answer":"My uncle set a goal to become a doctor. He made a great effort. He achieved his goal in 2020.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with successful and successfully.","options":[],"answer":"The school trip was successful. We completed the hike successfully.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one piece of advice with \"do your best\" or \"make an effort\".","options":[],"answer":"Always make an effort, even when it's difficult.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"achieve","match":"to succeed in doing something after trying hard","arabic":"يحقق"},{"word":"achievement","match":"something good that you succeed in doing","arabic":"إنجاز"},{"word":"goal","match":"something you want to do in the future","arabic":"هدف"},{"word":"effort","match":"hard work you put into doing something","arabic":"جهد"},{"word":"progress","match":"getting better at something","arabic":"تقدّم"},{"word":"award","match":"a prize for doing something well","arabic":"جائزة"},{"word":"medal","match":"a round piece of metal given as a prize","arabic":"ميدالية"},{"word":"certificate","match":"an official paper that shows you did something","arabic":"شهادة"},{"word":"skill","match":"the ability to do something well","arabic":"مهارة"},{"word":"practice","match":"doing something again and again to get better","arabic":"تدريب / ممارسة"},{"word":"succeed","match":"to do what you tried to do","arabic":"ينجح"},{"word":"success","match":"achieving what you wanted","arabic":"نجاح"},{"word":"challenge","match":"something difficult that tests your ability","arabic":"تحدٍّ"},{"word":"proud","match":"feeling happy about something you or someone else did","arabic":"فخور"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I need to ___ a decision about my summer course.","options":["take on","make","have","do"],"answer":"make","explanation":"make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"We ___ some research about solar energy.","options":["had","did","made","took"],"answer":"did","explanation":"do + your best / well / research / exercise.","explanation_ar":"do مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"Our team ___ a gold medal in the relay race.","options":["earned up","took up","won","gained"],"answer":"won","explanation":"Use the right achievement partner (set, achieve, win, earn).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"He was ___ in his exams.","options":["successful","successfully","succeed","success"],"answer":"successful","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."},{"q":"She finished the difficult puzzle ___.","options":["success","successful","successfully","succeed"],"answer":"successfully","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."},{"q":"Learning a new language is a real ___.","options":["challenged","challenger","challenge","challenging"],"answer":"challenge","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."},{"q":"My parents are ___ of my results.","options":["pride","prouded","proudly","proud"],"answer":"proud","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."},{"q":"","options":["I've had a lot of progress in swimming.","I've made a lot of progress in swimming.","I've done a lot of progress in swimming.","I've made a lot of progresses in swimming."],"answer":"I've made a lot of progress in swimming.","explanation":"make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"At the end of the course, everyone received a ___.","options":["certificate","medal race","challenge","progress"],"answer":"certificate","explanation":"Use the right achievement partner (set, achieve, win, earn).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Which collocation is correct?","options":["make a medal","do a goal","win a mistake","achieve a goal"],"answer":"achieve a goal","explanation":"Use the right achievement partner (set, achieve, win, earn).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A \"Wall of Achievement\" in a school corridor with certificates, medals, student photos and sticky notes saying \"Set a goal\", \"Make an effort\", \"Do your best\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A \"Wall of Achievement\" in a school corridor with certificates, medals, student photos and sticky notes saying \"Set a goal\", \"Make an effort\", \"Do your best\""},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows skill (the ability to do something well); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing skill: the ability to do something well"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows practice (doing something again and again to get better); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing practice: doing something again and again to get better"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows succeed (to do what you tried to do); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing succeed: to do what you tried to do"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows success (achieving what you wanted); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing success: achieving what you wanted"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows challenge (something difficult that tests your ability); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing challenge: something difficult that tests your ability"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows proud (feeling happy about something you or someone else did); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing proud: feeling happy about something you or someone else did"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W01","script":"skill. skill. Typing fast is a useful skill.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W02","script":"practice. practice. Practice makes perfect!","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W03","script":"succeed. succeed. If you keep trying, you will succeed.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W04","script":"success. success. The science fair was a big success.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W05","script":"challenge. challenge. Climbing the mountain was a real challenge.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-W06","script":"proud. proud. My parents are proud of my results.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Make Progress, Do Your Best: Achievement Collocations”. Let’s learn achievement words and collocations with make, do, win, achieve, set; word families (achieve → achievement; succeed → success → successful) together. Meet some new words. skill: the ability to do something well. practice: doing something again and again to get better. succeed: to do what you tried to do. make and do are often confused. make goes with: progress, an effort, a mistake, a decision, a plan, a difference. do goes with: your best, well, research, homework, exercise, a project. Other achievement partners: set a goal, achieve a goal, reach a goal, win an award / a medal / a prize, earn a certificate, face a challenge, develop a skill. Here are some examples. Rakan has made a lot of progress in English. Just do your best in the exam. Everyone makes mistakes – that's how we learn. Be careful! Some learners say: “I did a mistake.” That’s not right. We say: “I made a mistake.” mistake → make. Quick check: Do we \"make\" or \"do\" a mistake? … Think! … *make* a mistake. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"make progress\", \"do my best\" and \"achieve a goal\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4","title":"Because I Practiced. → Complete Sentences: Fixing Fragments","objectives":["Students will be able to identify sentence fragments.","Students will be able to fix fragments by adding a subject or verb or by joining them to a complete sentence.","I can tell a complete sentence from a fragment.","I can fix fragments in my writing."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على أشباه الجمل الناقصة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصحيحها بإضافة فاعل أو فعل أو بربطها بجملة كاملة.","أستطيع أن أميّز الجملة الكاملة من الجملة الناقصة.","أستطيع أن أصحح الجمل الناقصة في كتابتي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"achieve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈtʃiv/","definition":"to succeed in doing something after trying hard","arabic":"يحقق","example":"She achieved her dream of becoming a pilot.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"achievement","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈtʃivmənt/","definition":"something good that you succeed in doing","arabic":"إنجاز","example":"Finishing the marathon was a great achievement.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"goal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡoʊl/","definition":"something you want to do in the future","arabic":"هدف","example":"My goal is to read 30 books this year.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"effort","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛfɚt/","definition":"hard work you put into doing something","arabic":"جهد","example":"He made a big effort to improve his English.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"progress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɑˌɡrɛs/","definition":"getting better at something","arabic":"تقدّم","example":"You've made great progress in math.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"award","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈwɔrd/","definition":"a prize for doing something well","arabic":"جائزة","example":"Noura won an award for her short story.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A complete sentence has a subject, a verb and a complete idea: Faisal won a medal. A fragment is only part of a sentence, but it is written like a full sentence.\nCommon fragments: no subject ((not: Won a medal last year.)), no verb ((not: My brother and his team.)), a dependent clause alone ((not: Because I practiced every day.)), an -ing phrase alone ((not: Training three times a week.)).\nFix a fragment by adding what is missing (subject or verb) or by joining it to the sentence before or after: I won because I practiced every day.\ncomplete sentence = subject + verb + complete idea\nno subject / no verb → add it\nbecause/when/although/if + clause alone → join it to a main clause\n-ing phrase alone → add a subject and a verb","examples":["Faisal won a silver medal.","I passed the test because I studied hard.","When the results came out, we celebrated.","Lina is practicing every day for the competition.","My brother and his team won the cup.","We were proud of our project.","Although it was difficult, we finished on time.","She trains three times a week."],"common_errors":["✗ Because I was tired. → ✓ I went to bed early because I was tired. (A because-clause alone is a fragment.)","✗ Won the first prize. → ✓ Hamad won the first prize. (Add a subject.)","✗ My best friend and his brother. → ✓ My best friend and his brother play chess every Friday. (Add a verb and complete the idea.)","✗ Training every evening. → ✓ He is training every evening. (-ing phrase → add a subject and be.)"],"arabic":"الجملة الكاملة فيها فاعل وفعل وفكرة كاملة: Faisal won a medal.\nالجملة الناقصة (fragment) جزء من جملة كُتب كأنه جملة كاملة: Because I was tired.\nالتصحيح: نضيف الفاعل أو الفعل الناقص، أو نربط الجملة الناقصة بالجملة التي قبلها أو بعدها.\nفي العربية قد نحذف الفاعل أو الفعل أحيانًا، أما في الإنجليزية فالجملة تحتاج فاعلًا وفعلًا دائمًا."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Because I Practiced. → Complete Sentences: Fixing Fragments”. Let’s learn sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U2-LS4 | Because I Practiced. → Complete Sentences: Fixing Fragments","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A complete sentence has a subject, a verb and a complete idea: Faisal won a medal. A fragment is only part of a sentence, but it is written like a full sentence.","on_screen":"sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A complete sentence has a subject, a verb and a complete idea: Faisal won a medal. A fragment is only part of a sentence, but it is written like a full sentence. Common fragments: no subject ((not: Won a medal last year.)), no verb ((not: My brother and his team.)), a dependent clause alone ((not: Because I practiced every day.)), an -ing phrase alone ((not: Training three times a week.)).","on_screen":"complete sentence = subject + verb + complete idea • no subject / no verb → add it • because/when/although/if + clause alone → join it to a main clause","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Faisal won a silver medal. I passed the test because I studied hard. When the results came out, we celebrated.","on_screen":"Faisal won a silver medal. / I passed the test because I studied hard. / When the results came out, we celebrated.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Because I was tired.” That’s not right. We say: “I went to bed early because I was tired.” A because-clause alone is a fragment.","on_screen":"✗ Because I was tired.   ✓ I went to bed early because I was tired.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"When I got home.\" Is it a complete sentence? … Think! … No – it's a fragment. What happened when you got home? Great job! Now you can say: I can tell a complete sentence from a fragment.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can tell a complete sentence from a fragment.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الجملة الكاملة فيها فاعل وفعل وفكرة كاملة: Faisal won a medal.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Because I was tired. — الصحيح: I went to bed early because I was tired.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أميّز الجملة الكاملة من الجملة الناقصة."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Science Fair (editing passage)","body":"Our class entered the science fair. Built a solar oven. Because the sun is strong in Saudi Arabia. We tested it for two weeks. Cooking eggs and bread in it. The judges and the visitors. Winning second prize!","word_count":38,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the complete sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["Lina won the writing competition.","The writing competition and Lina.","Won the writing competition.","Because Lina won the writing competition."],"answer":"Lina won the writing competition.","explanation":"A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"","options":["The results and our celebration.","When the results came out.","We celebrated when the results came out.","Celebrating the results."],"answer":"We celebrated when the results came out.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"","options":["Because my cousin studying for his finals.","My cousin is studying for his finals.","Studying for his finals.","My cousin for his finals."],"answer":"My cousin is studying for his finals.","explanation":"An -ing phrase needs a subject and a verb (is/are).","explanation_ar":"عبارة ing تحتاج فاعلًا وفعلًا."},{"q":"","options":["Saad and Rakan.","Built a robot together.","Because Saad and Rakan built a robot.","Saad and Rakan built a robot."],"answer":"Saad and Rakan built a robot.","explanation":"Add the missing verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Although it was hard.","Although hard and not giving up.","Although it was hard, I didn't give up.","Didn't give up although hard."],"answer":"Although it was hard, I didn't give up.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"","options":["Gave us a certificate.","The coach gave us a certificate.","The coach and the certificate.","When the coach gave us a certificate."],"answer":"The coach gave us a certificate.","explanation":"Add the missing subject.","explanation_ar":"أضف الفاعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Is it a sentence (S) or a fragment (F)? Write S or F. Word bank: S, F","items":[{"q":"Because the bus was late. → ______","options":[],"answer":"F","explanation":"A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"The bus was late. → ______","options":[],"answer":"S","explanation":"A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"Practicing every day after school. → ______","options":[],"answer":"F","explanation":"An -ing phrase needs a subject and a verb (is/are).","explanation_ar":"عبارة ing تحتاج فاعلًا وفعلًا."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Fix the fragments.","items":[{"q":"I felt proud.  +  When I got my certificate.","options":[],"answer":"I felt proud when I got my certificate.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"She passed the exam.  +  Because she studied every day.","options":[],"answer":"She passed the exam because she studied every day.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"Running in the park every morning.  (add a subject and a verb)","options":[],"answer":"My dad is running in the park every morning.","explanation":"An -ing phrase needs a subject and a verb (is/are).","explanation_ar":"عبارة ing تحتاج فاعلًا وفعلًا."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the achievement report.","items":[{"q":"Our class entered the science fair. Built a solar oven. We chose it because the sun is strong in Saudi Arabia.","options":[],"answer":"Our class entered the science fair. We built a solar oven. We chose it because the sun is strong in Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Built → We built. A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Built → We built. الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"Our class entered the science fair. We built a solar oven. Because the sun is strong in Saudi Arabia.","options":[],"answer":"Our class entered the science fair. We built a solar oven. We chose it because the sun is strong in Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Because → We chose it because. A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Because → We chose it because. الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"We tested it for two weeks. Cooking eggs and bread in it. The judges and the visitors loved it. We won second prize!","options":[],"answer":"We tested it for two weeks. We cooked eggs and bread in it. The judges and the visitors loved it. We won second prize!","explanation":"Cooking eggs and bread in it. → We cooked eggs and bread in it.. A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Cooking eggs and bread in it. → We cooked eggs and bread in it.. الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"We tested it for two weeks. We cooked eggs and bread in it. The judges and the visitors. We won second prize!","options":[],"answer":"We tested it for two weeks. We cooked eggs and bread in it. The judges and the visitors loved it. We won second prize!","explanation":"The judges and the visitors. → The judges and the visitors loved it.. A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: The judges and the visitors. → The judges and the visitors loved it.. الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"We tested it for two weeks. We cooked eggs and bread in it. The judges and the visitors loved it. Winning second prize!","options":[],"answer":"We tested it for two weeks. We cooked eggs and bread in it. The judges and the visitors loved it. We won second prize!","explanation":"Winning second prize! → We won second prize!. A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Winning second prize! → We won second prize!. الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write complete sentences.","items":[{"q":"Turn this fragment into a sentence: \"After the long training.\"","options":[],"answer":"After the long training, the team was exhausted.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with because about an achievement.","options":[],"answer":"I won the race because I trained hard. My sister got a certificate because she finished the course.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence that starts with When and is complete.","options":[],"answer":"When I scored the goal, everyone cheered.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"achievement","clue":"something good that you succeed in doing"},{"word":"progress","clue":"getting better at something"},{"word":"success","clue":"achieving what you wanted"},{"word":"certificate","clue":"an official paper that shows you did something"},{"word":"challenge","clue":"something difficult that tests your ability"},{"word":"proud","clue":"feeling happy about something you or someone else did"},{"word":"achieve","clue":"to succeed in doing something after trying hard"},{"word":"goal","clue":"something you want to do in the future"},{"word":"effort","clue":"hard work you put into doing something"},{"word":"award","clue":"a prize for doing something well"},{"word":"medal","clue":"a round piece of metal given as a prize"},{"word":"skill","clue":"the ability to do something well"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["Our team and the match.","When our team won the match.","Won the match.","Our team won the match."],"answer":"Our team won the match.","explanation":"A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"Find the fragment.","options":["I wanted to improve, so I practiced.","I practiced because I wanted to improve.","Because I wanted to improve.","I wanted to improve."],"answer":"Because I wanted to improve.","explanation":"A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"What is missing in \"Wrote a story about a falcon.\"?","options":["a verb","a subject","a question mark","an object"],"answer":"a subject","explanation":"Add the missing subject.","explanation_ar":"أضف الفاعل."},{"q":"What is missing in \"My little sister and her friends.\"?","options":["a capital letter","a verb","a subject","a comma"],"answer":"a verb","explanation":"Add the missing verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["He is practicing the piano every day.","He practicing the piano every day.","Is practicing the piano every day.","Practicing the piano every day."],"answer":"He is practicing the piano every day.","explanation":"An -ing phrase needs a subject and a verb (is/are).","explanation_ar":"عبارة ing تحتاج فاعلًا وفعلًا."},{"q":"How can we fix \"When the bell rang.\"?","options":["The bell when rang.","When the bell. Rang we went out.","When the bell rang, we went out.","When the bell rang. We went out."],"answer":"When the bell rang, we went out.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"","options":["She was happy because she passed.","She was happy. Because she passed.","She was happy, because passed.","Because she passed."],"answer":"She was happy because she passed.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"","options":["My grandparents live in Abha.","Live in Abha.","My grandparents in Abha.","Because my grandparents live in Abha."],"answer":"My grandparents live in Abha.","explanation":"Add the missing verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف الفعل."},{"q":"Which one is a complete sentence?","options":["Although tired and finishing.","Although he was tired.","Finishing the race tired.","Although he was tired, he finished the race."],"answer":"Although he was tired, he finished the race.","explanation":"A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"","options":["Because we were proud of our project.","We proud of our project.","Proud of our project.","We were proud of our project."],"answer":"We were proud of our project.","explanation":"Add the missing verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف الفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Achievements” that shows sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Achievements” that shows sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them in action"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Because I Practiced. → Complete Sentences: Fixing Fragments”. Let’s learn sentence fragments (missing subject, missing verb, dependent clause alone, -ing phrase alone) and how to fix them together. A complete sentence has a subject, a verb and a complete idea: Faisal won a medal. A fragment is only part of a sentence, but it is written like a full sentence. A complete sentence has a subject, a verb and a complete idea: Faisal won a medal. A fragment is only part of a sentence, but it is written like a full sentence. Common fragments: no subject ((not: Won a medal last year.)), no verb ((not: My brother and his team.)), a dependent clause alone ((not: Because I practiced every day.)), an -ing phrase alone ((not: Training three times a week.)). Here are some examples. Faisal won a silver medal. I passed the test because I studied hard. When the results came out, we celebrated. Be careful! Some learners say: “Because I was tired.” That’s not right. We say: “I went to bed early because I was tired.” A because-clause alone is a fragment. Quick check: \"When I got home.\" Is it a complete sentence? … Think! … No – it's a fragment. What happened when you got home? Great job! Now you can say: I can tell a complete sentence from a fragment.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5","title":"My Achievements and Goals: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to talk about their achievements, progress and goals.","Students will be able to write an achievement report with the present perfect and complete sentences.","I can talk about my achievements and goals.","I can write a report about my progress."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التحدث عن إنجازاتهم وتقدمهم وأهدافهم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة تقرير عن الإنجازات بالمضارع التام وبجمل كاملة.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن إنجازاتي وأهدافي.","أستطيع أن أكتب تقريرًا عن تقدّمي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"achieve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈtʃiv/","definition":"to succeed in doing something after trying hard","arabic":"يحقق","example":"She achieved her dream of becoming a pilot.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"achievement","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈtʃivmənt/","definition":"something good that you succeed in doing","arabic":"إنجاز","example":"Finishing the marathon was a great achievement.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"goal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡoʊl/","definition":"something you want to do in the future","arabic":"هدف","example":"My goal is to read 30 books this year.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"effort","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛfɚt/","definition":"hard work you put into doing something","arabic":"جهد","example":"He made a big effort to improve his English.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"progress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɑˌɡrɛs/","definition":"getting better at something","arabic":"تقدّم","example":"You've made great progress in math.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"award","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈwɔrd/","definition":"a prize for doing something well","arabic":"جائزة","example":"Noura won an award for her short story.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"medal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛdəl/","definition":"a round piece of metal given as a prize","arabic":"ميدالية","example":"He won a gold medal in swimming.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"certificate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɚˈtɪfɪkət/","definition":"an official paper that shows you did something","arabic":"شهادة","example":"Every student received a certificate at the end of the course.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"skill","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skɪl/","definition":"the ability to do something well","arabic":"مهارة","example":"Typing fast is a useful skill.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"practice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpræktəs/","definition":"doing something again and again to get better","arabic":"تدريب / ممارسة","example":"Practice makes perfect!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"succeed","pos":"verb","ipa":"/səkˈsid/","definition":"to do what you tried to do","arabic":"ينجح","example":"If you keep trying, you will succeed.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"success","pos":"noun","ipa":"/səkˈsɛs/","definition":"achieving what you wanted","arabic":"نجاح","example":"The science fair was a big success.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"challenge","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃæləndʒ/","definition":"something difficult that tests your ability","arabic":"تحدٍّ","example":"Climbing the mountain was a real challenge.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"proud","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/praʊd/","definition":"feeling happy about something you or someone else did","arabic":"فخور","example":"My parents are proud of my results.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 2: the present perfect with for/since, just/already/yet, achievement collocations, word families and complete sentences.\nAn achievement report tells how long you've done something, what you've achieved, what you haven't done yet and your next goal.\n✔ for/since with the present perfect\n✔ just/already (positive) – yet (negative/question)\n✔ make progress, do your best, set/achieve a goal, win an award\n✔ complete sentences – no fragments","examples":["I've played the oud for two years.","I've already learned ten songs.","I haven't performed on stage yet.","My teacher says I've made great progress.","I set a goal to practice every day.","I've just received my first certificate!","I'm proud of my achievement.","I practiced every day because I wanted to improve."],"common_errors":["✗ I am in the club since September. → ✓ I've been in the club since September. (Past until now → present perfect.)","✗ I've done a lot of progress. → ✓ I've made a lot of progress. (make progress.)","✗ Because I practiced a lot. → ✓ I improved because I practiced a lot. (Join the fragment to a main clause.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المضارع التام مع for/since وjust/already/yet ومتلازمات الإنجاز والجمل الكاملة.\nتقرير الإنجاز يذكر: منذ متى، وماذا أنجزت، وماذا لم تنجز بعد، وما هدفك القادم.\nتذكّر: make progress وdo your best، ولا جمل ناقصة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Achievements and Goals: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U2-LS5 | My Achievements and Goals: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Award ceremony speeches: each student prepares a 30-second speech about one achievement – how long they've worked for it, what they've already done, what they haven't done yet and their next goal.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 2: the present perfect with for/since, just/already/yet, achievement collocations, word families and complete sentences. An achievement report tells how long you've done something, what you've achieved, what you haven't done yet and your next goal.","on_screen":"✔ for/since with the present perfect • ✔ just/already (positive) – yet (negative/question) • ✔ make progress, do your best, set/achieve a goal, win an award","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I've played the oud for two years. I've already learned ten songs. I haven't performed on stage yet.","on_screen":"I've played the oud for two years. / I've already learned ten songs. / I haven't performed on stage yet.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I am in the club since September.” That’s not right. We say: “I've been in the club since September.” Past until now → present perfect.","on_screen":"✗ I am in the club since September.   ✓ I've been in the club since September.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “I've done a lot of progress.”? … Think! … It should be “I've made a lot of progress.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about my achievements and goals.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about my achievements and goals.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المضارع التام مع for/since وjust/already/yet ومتلازمات الإنجاز والجمل الكاملة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I am in the club since September. — الصحيح: I've been in the club since September.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن إنجازاتي وأهدافي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Year in the Debate Club – Yusuf","body":"I have been a member of the school debate club since September.\nAt first, I was shy, but I've made a lot of progress.\nI've already taken part in three debates, and last month our team won an award for the best argument.\nI have also developed new skills, like listening carefully and speaking confidently.\nI haven't spoken at a national competition yet, but that is my next goal.\nI'll do my best and make an effort every week.\nI'm proud of my achievements this year!","word_count":86,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Yusuf's report. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Yusuf has been in the debate club since September.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Year in the Debate Club – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf was confident at first.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Year in the Debate Club – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"He has already taken part in three debates.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Year in the Debate Club – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His team won an award last month.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Year in the Debate Club – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf has already spoken at a national competition.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Year in the Debate Club – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf is proud of his achievements.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Year in the Debate Club – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Yusuf ___ a member of the club since September.","options":["is","was","has been","has being"],"answer":"has been","explanation":"Present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام."},{"q":"He has been in the club ___ September.","options":["from","since","ago","for"],"answer":"since","explanation":"for (period) / since (starting point).","explanation_ar":"for وsince."},{"q":"He has made a lot of ___.","options":["progress","mistakes good","effort a","progresses"],"answer":"progress","explanation":"Achievement collocation (make/do/win/set).","explanation_ar":"متلازمة الإنجاز."},{"q":"He hasn't spoken at a national competition ___.","options":["already","just","yet","since"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"Present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام."},{"q":"He speaks ___ now.","options":["confide","confidently","confidence","confident"],"answer":"confidently","explanation":"Word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"","options":["He improved. Because he practiced every week.","Practicing every week because improved.","Because he practiced every week.","He improved because he practiced every week."],"answer":"He improved because he practiced every week.","explanation":"Complete sentence (no fragment).","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Prepare your award speech. Write your notes.","items":[{"q":"My achievement: ___","options":[],"answer":"I won first place in the Quran recitation contest.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How long I've worked for it (for/since): ___","options":[],"answer":"I've practiced for two years.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I've already done: ___","options":[],"answer":"I've already memorized five juz'.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I haven't done yet: ___","options":[],"answer":"I haven't memorized the whole Quran yet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My next goal: ___","options":[],"answer":"My next goal is to memorize two more juz' this year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your achievement report.","items":[{"q":"Plan: achievement, for/since, already, yet, next goal, how you feel.","options":[],"answer":"reading club; since Grade 4; already read 40 books; haven't written a review in the magazine yet; read 60 books; proud","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your report in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"I've been in the reading club since Grade 4. I've read many interesting books. I've already read 40 books this year. I've made a lot of progress in my vocabulary. I haven't written a review for the school magazine yet. My next goal is to read 60 books. I'll do my best. I'm proud of my progress.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: present perfect? for/since? make/do? fragments? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"I have read since two years\" to \"I have read for two years\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"achieve","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"achievement","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"goal","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"effort","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"progress","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"award","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"medal","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"certificate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"skill","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"practice","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"succeed","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"success","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"challenge","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"proud","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I ___ the piano since I was six.","options":["played","am playing","have played","play"],"answer":"have played","explanation":"Present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام."},{"q":"She's been the team captain ___ two seasons.","options":["for","ago","from","since"],"answer":"for","explanation":"for (period) / since (starting point).","explanation_ar":"for وsince."},{"q":"Always ___ your best in exams.","options":["do","make","take","have"],"answer":"do","explanation":"Achievement collocation (make/do/win/set).","explanation_ar":"متلازمة الإنجاز."},{"q":"The project was very ___.","options":["success","successfully","successful","succeed"],"answer":"successful","explanation":"Word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"","options":["I've heard the good news just!","I've heard just the good news!","I just have heard the good news!","I've just heard the good news!"],"answer":"I've just heard the good news!","explanation":"Present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام."},{"q":"","options":["Celebrating because won.","We celebrated because our team won.","We celebrated. Because our team won.","Because our team won."],"answer":"We celebrated because our team won.","explanation":"Complete sentence (no fragment).","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة."},{"q":"My brother hasn't decided on a university ___.","options":["already","just","yet","since"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"Present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام."},{"q":"Everyone ___ mistakes when they learn something new.","options":["takes","makes","has","does"],"answer":"makes","explanation":"Achievement collocation (make/do/win/set).","explanation_ar":"متلازمة الإنجاز."},{"q":"","options":["How long are you a volunteer?","How long have you being a volunteer?","How long you have been a volunteer?","How long have you been a volunteer?"],"answer":"How long have you been a volunteer?","explanation":"Present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet.","explanation_ar":"المضارع التام."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for an achievement report:","options":["Making great progress since September.","I've made great progress since I joined the club in September.","I make great progress since I joined the club in September.","I've done great progress since I joined the club in September."],"answer":"I've made great progress since I joined the club in September.","explanation":"Achievement collocation (make/do/win/set).","explanation_ar":"متلازمة الإنجاز."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"An end-of-year award ceremony in the school hall: students receiving certificates on stage, proud parents clapping, and a banner with a falcon logo. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"An end-of-year award ceremony in the school hall: students receiving certificates on stage, proud parents clapping, and a banner with a falcon logo"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Achievements”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Achievements”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L05-U2-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS5-T1","script":"I have been a member of the school debate club since September. At first, I was shy, but I've made a lot of progress. I've already taken part in three debates, and last month our team won an award for the best argument. I have also developed new skills, like listening carefully and speaking confidently. I haven't spoken at a national competition yet, but that is my next goal. I'll do my best and make an effort every week. I'm proud of my achievements this year!","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Achievements and Goals: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present perfect with for/since/just/already/yet, achievement collocations, complete sentences (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Award ceremony speeches: each student prepares a 30-second speech about one achievement – how long they've worked for it, what they've already done, what they haven't done yet and their next goal. Today you use all of Unit 2: the present perfect with for/since, just/already/yet, achievement collocations, word families and complete sentences. An achievement report tells how long you've done something, what you've achieved, what you haven't done yet and your next goal. Here are some examples. I've played the oud for two years. I've already learned ten songs. I haven't performed on stage yet. Be careful! Some learners say: “I am in the club since September.” That’s not right. We say: “I've been in the club since September.” Past until now → present perfect. Quick check: what is wrong with “I've done a lot of progress.”? … Think! … It should be “I've made a lot of progress.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about my achievements and goals.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"My parents ___ married for twenty years.","options":["have been","have be","were","are"],"answer":"have been","explanation":"Started in the past and continues now → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"من الماضي حتى الآن ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"I've known my teacher ___ Grade 3.","options":["from","since","ago","for"],"answer":"since","explanation":"since + a starting point.","explanation_ar":"since مع نقطة البداية."},{"q":"We've waited here ___ an hour!","options":["from","for","since","ago"],"answer":"for","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."},{"q":"","options":["How long do you have this bike?","How long have you have this bike?","How long you have had this bike?","How long have you had this bike?"],"answer":"How long have you had this bike?","explanation":"How long + have/has + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How long."},{"q":"","options":["I lived in Jeddah since I was born.","I live in Jeddah since I was born.","I've lived in Jeddah since I was born.","I've lived in Jeddah for I was born."],"answer":"I've lived in Jeddah since I was born.","explanation":"Started in the past and continues now → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"من الماضي حتى الآن ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"I've ___ finished the test. Can I leave now?","options":["just","since","yet","ever"],"answer":"just","explanation":"just = a short time ago (have + just + past participle).","explanation_ar":"just للتو."},{"q":"Has your brother called ___?","options":["ever since","just","already","yet"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"She has ___ won three medals this year.","options":["yet","since","already","ever"],"answer":"already","explanation":"already = sooner than expected (have + already + past participle).","explanation_ar":"already بالفعل."},{"q":"","options":["We haven't decided yet where to go.","We haven't decided where to go yet.","We didn't decide yet where to go.","We have decided where to go yet."],"answer":"We haven't decided where to go yet.","explanation":"yet = until now, at the end of negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"yet في النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"","options":["I've met the new student just.","I've just met the new student.","I've met just the new student.","I just have met the new student."],"answer":"I've just met the new student.","explanation":"Put just/already before the past participle; yet at the end.","explanation_ar":"مكان الكلمة."},{"q":"Don't worry if you ___ a mistake. Try again.","options":["do","take","make","have"],"answer":"make","explanation":"make + progress / an effort / a mistake / a decision.","explanation_ar":"make مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"Did you ___ your best in the race?","options":["make","give","do","have"],"answer":"do","explanation":"do + your best / well / research / exercise.","explanation_ar":"do مع هذه الكلمات."},{"q":"Our school ___ an award for recycling.","options":["won","gained","took","earned up"],"answer":"won","explanation":"Use the right achievement partner (set, achieve, win, earn).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The festival was a big ___.","options":["success","successfully","succeed","successful"],"answer":"success","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."},{"q":"She passed all her exams ___.","options":["successful","succeed","success","successfully"],"answer":"successfully","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form (verb, noun, adjective, adverb).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة من العائلة."},{"q":"Choose the correct word partnership.","options":["win a progress","set a goal","make a medal","do a goal"],"answer":"set a goal","explanation":"Use the right achievement partner (set, achieve, win, earn).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["My team well and won.","Because my team played well and won.","Played well and won.","My team played well and won."],"answer":"My team played well and won.","explanation":"A fragment is not a complete sentence.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الناقصة ليست جملة كاملة."},{"q":"Which group of words is not a complete sentence?","options":["When the competition started.","When the competition started, we were nervous.","We were nervous when the competition started.","The competition started."],"answer":"When the competition started.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"What is missing in \"Studied all night for the exam.\"?","options":["a comma","an object","a verb","a subject"],"answer":"a subject","explanation":"Add the missing subject.","explanation_ar":"أضف الفاعل."},{"q":"","options":["Training for the marathon.","He training for the marathon.","Is training for the marathon.","He is training for the marathon."],"answer":"He is training for the marathon.","explanation":"An -ing phrase needs a subject and a verb (is/are).","explanation_ar":"عبارة ing تحتاج فاعلًا وفعلًا."},{"q":"How can we fix \"Because the weather was bad.\"?","options":["Because, the weather was bad.","The weather because was bad.","The match was canceled because the weather was bad.","Because the weather was bad, canceled."],"answer":"The match was canceled because the weather was bad.","explanation":"Join the dependent clause to a main clause.","explanation_ar":"اربط الجملة التابعة بجملة رئيسة."},{"q":"Which sentence would be best in a progress report?","options":["Practicing karate for four years and earning a black belt.","I practice karate since four years, and I just earn my black belt.","I have practiced karate for four years, and I've just earned my black belt.","I have practiced karate since four years, and I've earned just my black belt."],"answer":"I have practiced karate for four years, and I've just earned my black belt.","explanation":"for + a period of time.","explanation_ar":"for مع المدة."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"i know him for ten years.\"","options":["I've known him since ten years.","I've known him for ten years.","I know him for ten years.","i've known him for ten years."],"answer":"I've known him for ten years.","explanation":"Started in the past and continues now → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"من الماضي حتى الآن ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"Have you finished your project yet? – ___","options":["Yes, I've already finished it.","Yes, I already finish it yesterday.","Yes, I've just finish it.","Yes, I've finished it yet."],"answer":"Yes, I've already finished it.","explanation":"already = sooner than expected (have + already + past participle).","explanation_ar":"already بالفعل."}],"theme_ar":"الإنجازات","essential_question_ar":"ماذا يتطلب تحقيق هدف ما؟","can_do":"I can talk about achievements and progress with the present perfect, for, since, just, already and yet, and write complete sentences.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الإنجازات والتقدّم بالمضارع التام وfor وsince وjust وalready وyet، وأكتب جملًا كاملة."});
